{# ==============================================================================
# Grid Engine Executor: PAM Authorization Configuration
# ==============================================================================
#
# This Jinja2 template generates the PAM configuration file for Grid Engine's
# authorization module (pam_sge_authorize.so).
#
# Grid Engine (Sun Grid Engine / Oracle Grid Engine / Univa Grid Engine) uses
# PAM (Pluggable Authentication Modules) to validate user access to compute
# nodes. The module `pam_sge_authorize.so` checks if a user is permitted to
# run jobs on the specific executor node based on the Grid Engine configuration
# (qconf commands) and group memberships.
#
# This file is typically sourced by the system's PAM stack (e.g., sshd, rsh,
# or dedicated grid authentication services) during job execution login.
# ============================================================================== #}

# PAM configuration file for Grid Engine authorization
# This file is sourced by the system PAM configuration for Grid Engine

# The pam_sge_authorize.so module performs the following checks:
# 1. Verifies if the user is defined in the Grid Engine configuration.
# 2. Checks if the user is a member of the 'sgeadmin' group (if applicable).
# 3. Validates against the 'allowed_users' or 'allowed_hosts' lists defined
#    in the cluster's qmaster and executor configurations.
#
# Arguments:
#   - silent: (Optional) If present, suppresses error messages to the user
#             when authorization fails. This is commonly used to allow
#             generic SSH prompts while Grid Engine handles the actual check.
#   - debug: (Optional) Enables debug logging to syslog. Useful for troubleshooting
#            authorization failures. Not recommended for production.

# Default behavior: Required authentication using the SGE PAM module.
# No specific arguments are strictly required by the module for standard operation,
# but 'silent' is a common best practice to avoid exposing SGE-specific errors
# to end-users during SSH login attempts for job submission.

auth required pam_sge_authorize.so {# silent #}
